\description{
Executes the complete three-pillar performance-assessment workflow in a
single call:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Connectivity & Many-Facet Measurement}: Verifies multi-facet
graph connectivity and fits \code{RSM}, \code{PCM}, or a Generalized Many-Facet Rasch Model
(GMFRM, selected with \code{model = "GPCM"}) via \code{MML},
\code{JML}, \code{JML_jeffreys}, or \code{CML} in C++ (\code{EAP} and Warm's \code{WLE}, optional
dynamic Markov rater drift via \code{occasion}, \code{step_constraints},
\code{category_support}, and explanatory \code{facet_formulas}).
\item \strong{G-Study & D-Study Planning}: Decomposes observed rating variance
(\code{urGENOVA} Henderson Method 1 across crossed, nested, and multivariate
composite designs) and identifies minimal designs meeting target \eqn{G} and \eqn{\Phi}{Phi}.
\item \strong{Rater Diagnostics, Fair(M), Real SE, Bias, & DFF Screening}:
Flags noisy/central/severe raters, computes \code{RajuSA-Welch} pairwise bias,
extracts unexpected ratings, and optionally screens group-level DFF and cutoffs.
}
}
